<div class="unit-details" id="overview">

    <!-- Overview & Objectives Split -->
    <div class="grid-2-col">
        <!-- Unit Overview -->
        <div class="content-box">
            <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-binoculars"></i> Unit Overview</h2>
            <p style="font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.5;">Your online world is part of your real world. In this
                unit, you’ll discover how your digital identity is created, what your online actions reveal about you,
                and how your choices can protect—or harm—your privacy and wellbeing. You’ll explore how platforms track
                data, how misinformation spreads, why digital footprints matter, and how to build a positive online
                presence.</p>
        </div>

        <!-- Unit Objectives -->
        <div class="content-box">
            <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-bullseye"></i> Unit Objectives</h2>
            <ul class="custom-list">
                <li>Understand online security, privacy, and digital citizenship.</li>
                <li>Recognise harmful digital behaviours and how online actions affect reputation and wellbeing.</li>
                <li>Explore how digital footprints are created and maintained.</li>
                <li>Undertake creative digital projects across multiple applications.</li>
                <li>Reflect on personal online identity and responsible participation online.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Concepts -->
    <div class="content-box">
        <h2 class="content-title"><i class="fa-solid fa-lightbulb"></i> Concepts</h2>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">This unit focuses on three SGS Computer Science concepts:</p>

        <div class="concepts-grid">
            <div class="concept-card">
                <h3 class="concept-name"><i class="fa-solid fa-rocket"></i> Innovation</h3>
                <p class="concept-def">How new technologies influence the way people communicate, behave online, and
                    build digital identities.</p>
                <p class="concept-context"><strong>In this unit:</strong> we explore how platforms shape the way we
                    present ourselves and how digital tools create new forms of identity.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="concept-card">
                <h3 class="concept-name"><i class="fa-solid fa-fingerprint"></i> Adaptation</h3>
                <p class="concept-def">How digital identities change over time and how online behaviour responds to
                    platform norms and digital footprints.</p>
                <p class="concept-context"><strong>In this unit:</strong> we look at how your online presence evolves
                    and how everyday actions leave lasting traces.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="concept-card">
                <h3 class="concept-name"><i class="fa-solid fa-database"></i> Data</h3>
                <p class="concept-def">How information about you—posts, likes, searches, and hidden metadata—is
                    collected, stored, and interpreted.</p>
                <p class="concept-context"><strong>In this unit:</strong> we examine how digital footprints are created
                    and what your online trail tells others about you.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

